\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Exact finite-system mean-field Potts calculations with the exact reservoir at the secant calibration. Points are occupation sums and Gamma/Beta CDF evaluations, connected to guide the eye. Dotted lines are the proved secant boundary limits for $c_N=\gamma N^{3/2}$, with $\gamma =0.5$ and $2$. Only these two sequences extend to $N=12000$; the others stop at $N=6000$. These are mean-field data and do not test a short-range interfacial law.}}{28}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:potts-scaling}{{1}{28}{Exact finite-system mean-field Potts calculations with the exact reservoir at the secant calibration. Points are occupation sums and Gamma/Beta CDF evaluations, connected to guide the eye. Dotted lines are the proved secant boundary limits for $c_N=\gamma N^{3/2}$, with $\gamma =0.5$ and $2$. Only these two sequences extend to $N=12000$; the others stop at $N=6000$. These are mean-field data and do not test a short-range interfacial law}{figure.1}{}}
